#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""fluxx: consistent product and brand pictures with FLUX 3 Image Klein on a Google Colab GPU.

Every `gen` is one GPU lifetime: colab new -> install diffusers -> load FLUX 3 Klein -> render every
shot -> download the pictures -> colab stop. The GPU never outlives the command (try/finally,
SIGTERM/SIGHUP handlers, and a detached watchdog that stops it after --max-minutes).

  fluxx login                      sign in to Google (Colab) and save a Hugging Face token, once
  fluxx doctor                     what is set up and what is still missing
  fluxx brand new NAME [--business .. --style .. --avoid .. --aspect 4:5]
  fluxx brand ref NAME IMAGE [--role product|style]    add a reference picture
  fluxx brand show NAME | list
  fluxx gen -b NAME [-n 2] [--aspect 1:1] [--draft] "scene" ["scene" ...]   (or --from FILE)
  fluxx rate SHOT good|bad ["why"]  feedback the brand learns from
  fluxx stop | status | selftest

Pictures land in ~/colab-flux/brands/NAME/shots/<time>/ as <id>_hd.png (about 4 MP) and
<id>_md.jpg (1024 px long side). Progress and the cost line go to stderr.
"""
from __future__ import annotations

